.TH BATCH 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
batch \- schedule a command for execution when system load permits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B batch
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B batch
reads a shell command script from standard input and submits it as a
job to be run as soon as the system's load allows, equivalent to
.RB \` "at \-q b \-m now" \' .
As with
.BR at (1),
submission only queues the job in the spool for
.BR atd (1)
to actually execute later; the submitted time is the moment
.B batch
is invoked.
.PP
On successful submission, a decimal job identifier and the submission
time are printed to standard error as
"\fBjob\fR \fIid\fR \fBat\fR \fItime\fR".
.PP
Once a job submitted this way becomes due (immediately, since it is
submitted for "now"),
.BR atd (1)
defers actually starting it for as long as the system's one\-minute
load average is at or above 1.5, retrying on each subsequent poll,
matching
.BR batch (1p) 's
own "run using algorithms, based on unspecified factors" wording. On a
platform with no load\-average facility to consult, this deferral does
not apply, and the job runs at the next poll after submission.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH OPERANDS
None. Any operand is refused as unexpected.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The job was successfully submitted.
.TP
.B 1
An unexpected operand was given, or the job could not be submitted
(e.g. the job spool could not be accessed).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR at (1),
.BR atd (1),
.BR crontab (1),
.BR crond (1)
